      "content": "#include <cstdio>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n\nclass FastScanner {\n    static constexpr int BUFSIZE = 1 << 20;\n    int idx = 0;\n    int size = 0;\n    char buf[BUFSIZE];\npublic:\n    inline char getChar() {\n        if (idx >= size) {\n            size = (int)fread(buf, 1, BUFSIZE, stdin);\n            idx = 0;\n            if (size == 0) return '\\0';\n        }\n        return buf[idx++];\n    }\n\n    int nextInt() {\n        char c;\n        do { c = getChar(); } while (c <= ' ');\n        int sign = 1;\n        if (c == '-') {\n            sign = -1;\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        int x = 0;\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = getChar();\n        }\n        return sign * x;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner fs;\n    int n = fs.nextInt();\n    int s = fs.nextInt();\n\n    const size_t ringSize = (size_t)s + 1;\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> ring(new int[ringSize * (size_t)n]);\n    std::vector<long long> col(n, 0);\n    std::vector<long long> pref(n + 1);\n\n    // Read first s rows and accumulate column sums.\n    for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n        int* row = &ring[(size_t)r * n];\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            row[j] = v;\n            col[j] += v;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Prefix sums of column totals.\n    pref[0] = 0;\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) pref[j + 1] = pref[j] + col[j];\n\n    long long best = pref[s];  // window starting at column 0\n    int limit = n - s;\n\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n    for (int j = 1; j <= limit; ++j) {\n        long long wsum = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\n        if (wsum > best) best = wsum;\n    }\n\n    size_t outSlot = 0;\n    size_t inSlot = s % ringSize;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= limit; ++i) {\n        int* pout = &ring[outSlot * n];\n        int* pin = &ring[inSlot * n];\n\n        // Update column sums and store the new row, unrolled by 4.\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < n; j += 4) {\n            int v0 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v1 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v2 = fs.nextInt();\n            int v3 = fs.nextInt();\n            pin[j] = v0; col[j] += (long long)v0 - pout[j];\n            pin[j + 1] = v1; col[j + 1] += (long long)v1 - pout[j + 1];\n            pin[j + 2] = v2; col[j + 2] += (long long)v2 - pout[j + 2];\n            pin[j + 3] = v3; col[j + 3] += (long long)v3 - pout[j + 3];\n        }\n        for (; j < n; ++j) {\n            int v = fs.nextInt();\n            pin[j] = v;\n            col[j] += (long long)v - pout[j];\n        }\n\n        // Recompute prefix sums of the updated column totals.\n        pref[0] = 0;\n        for (int k = 0; k < n; ++k) pref[k + 1] = pref[k] + col[k];\n\n#pragma GCC ivdep\n        for (int j = 0; j <= limit; ++j) {\n            long long wsum = pref[j + s] - pref[j];\n            if (wsum > best) best = wsum;\n        }\n\n        // Advance ring slots with wrap-around.\n        if (++outSlot == ringSize) outSlot = 0;\n        if (++inSlot == ringSize) inSlot = 0;\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Replacing modulo-based ring indexing with conditional wrap-around pointers, unrolling the per-row column-sum update loop by four, and computing horizontal window maxima via a prefix-sum array (which allows independent vectorizable iterations) should reduce loop overhead and improve instruction-level parallelism on the 4-core ARM64 target.",
  "notes": "The streaming ring-buffer approach is retained to limit memory usage. The prefix-sum method replaces the sequential sliding-window accumulation, enabling better auto-vectorization of the max-finding loops. Unrolling reduces branch and function-call overhead in the hot read/update loop.",
